<BaseLayout title="Medical disclaimer" description="Important limits, emergency guidance, and appropriate use of stretchesfor."><article class="container-shell py-14 sm:py-20"><div class="max-w-3xl"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-danger">Read before using the tool</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-balance text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-6xl">Medical disclaimer</h1><p class="mt-5 text-pretty text-lg leading-8 text-muted">stretchesfor provides general educational information. It does not provide medical diagnosis, treatment, or emergency services.</p></div><div class="prose-sf mt-14 max-w-3xl"><h2>Do not rely on this site in an emergency</h2><p>If you have severe or rapidly worsening symptoms, trouble breathing, chest pressure, fainting, stroke-like symptoms, major trauma, uncontrolled bleeding, or another emergency concern, contact your local emergency service now.</p><h2>No diagnosis</h2><p>Names of conditions and patterns are possibilities people may encounter, not conclusions about your symptoms. A short browser questionnaire cannot perform a physical examination, review your full history, order testing, or rule out every serious cause.</p><h2>Stop guidance</h2><p>Stop any movement that causes worsening pain, sharp or spreading pain, numbness, tingling, weakness, dizziness, breathlessness, or a new symptom. Seek professional advice if pain persists, recurs, disrupts daily activity, or concerns you.</p><h2>Personal advice takes priority</h2><p>If guidance here conflicts with advice from a healthcare professional who knows your circumstances, follow that professional’s advice.</p><h2>Use at your own discretion</h2><p>Exercise suitability varies with age, health conditions, pregnancy, recent surgery, medication, injury history, and other factors that this tool cannot fully assess. When uncertain, choose professional evaluation.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
